# KEUR-DOC-003 — command-token drift between docs (PARKED: needs ADR-022 engine).
# @implements ADR-061
#
# PARKED (.rule.parked, inert) because it needs the `cross-reference` engine
# (ADR-022, proposed) which does not exist yet. keur's current engines are all
# single-file (pattern/presence/absence) or whole-fileset-existence
# (file-absence/presence); none can assert "set A (commands in AGENTS/README) ⊆
# set B (commands in CONTRIBUTING)". That subset check across two files is
# exactly what ADR-022's corpus-scoped engine is for.
#
# Intended behaviour once the engine lands: extract build/test command tokens
# (make <target>, npm run <x>, pnpm <x>) from AGENTS.md and README.md; require
# each to also appear in CONTRIBUTING.md (the owner, ADR-061). A command named
# in an agent-facing file but NOT in the human reference means they have drifted
# or contradict — the single worst doc failure, because an agent follows the
# stale literal confidently. The finding names both files and the orphan token.
#
# This file is kept as the design-of-record so the rule is ready to activate by
# renaming .rule.parked -> .rule the day the cross-reference engine exists.
id: KEUR-DOC-003
ilities: [analysability, modifiability]
maturity: 3
title: Build/test command in AGENTS/README not found in CONTRIBUTING (drift/contradiction)
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: cross-reference
action: warn
# ADR-022 draft shape (fields are illustrative until the engine fixes them):
#   source_files: AGENTS.md README.md
#   target_file: CONTRIBUTING.md
#   extract: '\b(make\s+[a-z-]+|npm run [a-z:-]+|pnpm [a-z:-]+)\b'
#   assert: subset           # every source token must appear in target
target:
  filenames: AGENTS.md README.md
confidence: 0.6
message: "A build/test command named in AGENTS.md or README.md does not appear in CONTRIBUTING.md. CONTRIBUTING owns operational commands (ADR-061); a command only in an agent/human-facing file means they have drifted — an agent will run the stale one. Move the command's owner to CONTRIBUTING and link to it."
fix: "Put the authoritative command in CONTRIBUTING.md and have AGENTS.md/README.md reference it. One owner per fact; repeat links, not facts."
